    "question": "What is the dual-package hazard?",
    "quickAnswer": "The dual-package hazard occurs when CommonJS and ESM load two copies of the same package. The process then has separate module identities and potentially separate singleton state.",
    "conceptualExplanation": "Different resolution paths select different exports, so caches and identity-based comparisons no longer refer to one shared module instance.",
    "productionTradeOff": "Conditional exports improve compatibility, but require explicit integration tests and careful control of stateful dependencies.",
